 "equipment_type": "Air-cooled split condensing unit controller",
 "applies_to": "Carrier 38APS and 38APD 025-130 air-cooled condensing units with ComfortLink controls and the factory UPC Open BACnet option.",
 "summary": "On 38APS/38APD condensing units the BACnet option is a UPC Open controller in the main control box. It talks BACnet MS/TP to the BMS and CCN to the unit's ComfortLink board. The list has about 150 objects: start/stop, emergency stop, demand limit, cooling setpoints, control mode and type, compressor and fan relays, circuit pressures and temperatures, run hours and starts, thermostat inputs and spare user values.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": "ComfortLink v8",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Object names end in _1, except a few printed without it (stat, oa_temp, space_temp, comm_lost_alm).",
  "Multistate objects (MSV) are copies of CCN points made for i-Vu and BACnet; their state numbers are printed from 0, so the device may report them +1 (BACnet multistate values start at 1). Check by discovery.",
  "Binary states are shown as 0/1 from the printed ON_OFF, YES_NO and ENA_DIS ranges. Numeric ranges are added to descriptions.",
  "Rows appear for both circuits (A and B) with the same description; the object name tells them apart.",
  "The 5 user-defined analog and 5 binary values are spare objects with no unit function."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "38APS/38APD 025-130 Air-Cooled Condensing Units with ComfortLink Controls Version 8 - Controls, Start-Up, Operation, Service and Troubleshooting (Appendix C, Table G Network Points List)",
  "doc_number": "38AP-3T",
  "revision_date": "2022-08 (Rev A)",
  "url": "https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1005/Public/02/38AP-3T.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Address the UPC Open on its rotary switches and set the BAS port DIP switches for MS/TP. Set the unit control method to CCN Control (CTRL=3); the BMS then starts and stops the unit with BV 4 chil_s_s_1 and can limit capacity with AV 2 dem_lim_1. Read the control mode (AV 8), capacity, circuit pressures and the comm alarm.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 4",
    "name": "chil_s_s_1",
    "why": "Start/stop command (CCN control only)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 2",
    "name": "dem_lim_1",
    "why": "Active demand limit, %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 5",
    "name": "ctrl_pnt_1",
    "why": "Control point"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 5",
    "name": "control_msv_1",
    "why": "Control method: must be CCN for BMS start/stop"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 8",
    "name": "stat",
    "why": "Control mode (6 = On CCN, 2 = Off CCN)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3",
    "name": "cap_t_1",
    "why": "Percent total capacity"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 1008",
    "name": "sa_temp_1",
    "why": "Supply air temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 1",
    "name": "alm_msv_1",
    "why": "Alarm state: Normal, Alert or Alarm"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 58",
    "name": "comm_lost_alm",
    "why": "UPC Open lost CCN communication with the unit"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "Set the control method to CCN Control (Configuration > OPT2 > CTRL = 3); the manual says units run by a third-party BAS through the UPC Open must use it. The unit switch must be in Enable, or in Remote Control with the external contacts closed. The BMS then writes CHIL_S_S Start/Stop; EMSTOP (BV 6) stops all cooling until set back to Enable.",
  "heartbeat": "The manual says loss of CCN communication puts the unit in stand-alone mode. BV 58 comm_lost_alm and BV 2999 element_stat_1 show the UPC Open link to the unit.",
  "remote_sensors": "Outside Air Temperature (AV 1003) and Space Temperature (AV 2007) are writable; the space temperature is used with the SPT control types.",
  "setup": [
   "Set the MAC address on the UPC Open Tens and Ones rotary switches; it reads switches, DIP switches and jumpers only at power-up.",
   "Device instance = network number (default 16101) followed by the MAC address, e.g. MAC 20 gives 1610120.",
   "BAS port: DS3 enable, DS4 E1-485, DS5-DS8 set to MSTP; baud on DS1-DS2 (9600, 19.2k, 38.4k or 76.8k, Carrier default 76.8k); 8N1 fixed. EIA-485 jumpers to EIA-485 and 2W.",
   "Fit a BT485 terminator on the first and last controller of the MS/TP segment.",
   "The UPC Open and the ComfortLink board must use the same CCN element and bus numbers (factory 1 and 0)."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Start/stop over BACnet only works with the control method set to CCN; monitoring alone does not need it.",
   "Points depend on unit size and options (number of compressors and fans, head pressure control, digital compressor).",
   "Thermostat inputs Y1-Y4 are read-only in this list."
  ]
 },
